    "title": "Environmental Sustainability: Water Conservation and Waste Management",
    "summary": "This page outlines SBI's environmental sustainability initiatives in water conservation and waste management. For water, it notes minimal consumption limited to drinking and municipal use, with no significant community impact. It reports FY25 water consumption (15,67,890 KL) and discharge (12,54,312 KL), sourcing mainly from municipal supplies or third-party vendors (withdrawal 28,22,203 KL). Initiatives include rainwater harvesting at 542 locations, 30 sewage treatment plants, and recycling 118,768.3 KL of water. For waste management, it describes the 3R approach, focusing on paper and e-waste reduction through digitalization and Green Banking. It includes an e-waste policy, awareness sessions, and clean-up drives. A data table details FY25 and FY24 waste generated, recycled, and disposed for plastic, paper, e-waste, battery, and food waste, with notes on disposal methods.",
}
